<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flemish Baroque painting</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1585–<a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flemish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> painting is the art of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-netherlands">Southern Netherlands</a> from the late sixteenth to the late seventeenth century, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-paul-rubens">Peter Paul Rubens</a>, with Anthony van Dyck, Jacob Jordaens and Frans Snyders, it produced large altarpieces for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a> churches, portraits, still lifes and landscapes. Rubens's workshop and the city's art market made Antwerp one of the main artistic centres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flemish-baroque-painting.jpg" alt="Flemish Baroque painting" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Paul Rubens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_De_kruisoprichting.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
